2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelia (wife of Aemilius Paullus)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelia (around 46 BC-16 BC) was the daughter of Scribonia and consul Publius Cornelius Scipio Salvito. She was married twice. Her first husband was Sextus Julius Caesar III. Together they had one son born in 32 BC, named Sextus 
2 CONC Julius Caesar IV. Her second husband was the censor Lucius Aemilius Paullus. Their first son Lucius Aemilius Paullus married his cousin Julia the Younger and their second son Marcus Aemilius Lepidus was consul in 6. She also had a
2 CONC  daughter called Aemilia Paulla born in 22 BC who married Publius Memmius Regulus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelia was the sister of Cornelius Scipio, and was the elder half-sister of Julia the Elder. Cornelia died in the same year of her brother's consulship; if this brother is identified as P. Cornelius Scipio, the date was 16 BC Em
2 CONC peror Augustus, her stepfather, grieved her death as he found her a worthy elder sister to his daughter, Julia. The poet Propertius wrote an elegy of Cornelia for her funeral, praising her virtue and family, including Scipio and S
2 CONC cribonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornelia_(wife_of_Aemilius_Paullus)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelia (wife of Aemilius Paullus)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Cornelia Scipio)
2 CONT
2 CONT This article does not cite any references or sources. Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unsourced material may be challenged and removed. (April 2009)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelia (around 46 BC-16 BC) was the daughter of Scribonia and consul Publius Cornelius Scipio Salvito. She was married twice. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first husband was Sextus Julius Caesar III. Together they had one son born in 32 BC, named 
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Sextus Julius Caesar IV. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second husband was the censor Lucius Aemilius Paullus. Their first son 
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Lucius Aemilius Paullus married his cousin Julia the Younger and their second son 
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Marcus Aemilius Lepidus was consul in 6. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She also had a daughter called 
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Aemilia Paulla born in 22 BC who married Publius Memmius Regulus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelia was the sister of Cornelius Scipio, and was the elder half-sister of Julia the Elder. Cornelia died in the same year of her brother's consulship; if this brother is identified as P. Cornelius Scipio, the date was 16 BC Em
2 CONC peror Augustus, her stepfather, grieved her death as he found her a worthy elder sister to his daughter, Julia. The poet Propertius wrote an elegy of Cornelia for her funeral, praising her virtue and family, including Scipio and S
2 CONC cribonia.
