1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_the_Elder
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Julia the Elder''', born 39 B.C to '''Augustus''' and '''Scribonia'''. She had three marriages. She married at the age of fourteen (1) '''M. Marcellus''', son of Octavia, (Julia persuaded Octavia to allow the divorce of her son
2 CONC  in order for this marriage to take place), but there was no issue, and two years after the marriage, Marcellus died. She then married in 21 B.C. (2) '''M. Vipsanius Agrippa''', who had been persuaded by the Emperor to obtain a di
2 CONC vorce from his wife. Julia was eighteen and Agrippa forty-two. She finally married in 9 B.C. (3) '''Tiberius''', son of Livia (forced to obtain a divorce from his pregnant wife, Vipsania Agrippina, daughter of Agrippa), with no is
2 CONC sue. Julia is reported to have had many illicit affairs along with her formal marriages. As a result her father, the Emperor, finally was forced to banish her to the island of Pandateria. One of her lovers, a son of Antony, was fo
2 CONC rced to kill himself, and several others were exiled. After sixteen years of imprisonment, she died.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
