1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aufidia
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopediaJump to:navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aufidia or Alfidia (flourished 1st century BC), was a Roman Matron. Aufidia was a daughter to Roman Magistrate Marcus Aufidius Lurco and her mother is unknown. She was a member of the gens Aufidia, a Roman family of Plebs status, 
2 CONC who appeared in the Roman Republic and Roman Empire. They became a family of consular rank. Her father originally came from Fundi (modern Fondi, Italy).
2 CONT
2 CONT She married the future praetor, Marcus Livius Drusus Claudianus. They had at least two children: a daughter Livia Drusilla (58 BC-29) and a son Marcus Livius Drusus, who served as a Roman consul. Livia was to become the first Roma
2 CONC n Empress and third wife of the first Roman Emperor Augustus. Aufidia would be the maternal grandmother to Roman Emperor Tiberius Claudius Nero and Roman General Nero Claudius Drusus. The Roman Emperors Caligula, Claudius and Nero
2 CONC  were her direct descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aufidia
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Note: She married the future praetor, Marcus LIvius Drusus Claudianus. They had at least two children: a daughter Livia Drusilla (58 BC-29) and a son Marcus Livius Drusus, who served as a Roman consul. Livia was to become the firs
2 CONC t Roman Empress and third wife of the first Roman Emperor Augustus. Aufidia would be the maternal grandmother to Roman Emperor Tiberius Claudius Nero and Roman General Nero Glaudius Drusus. The Roman Emperors Caligula, Claudius an
2 CONC d Nero were her direct descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 142 BC in Latium
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT iNFO FROM http://www.genealogy4u.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I124159&tree=western2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Aufidia or Alfidia was a Roman Matron who lived in the first century BC and was the mother to the first Roman Empress Livia Drusilla. Livia Drusilla was the third wife to the first Roman Emperor Caesar Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aufidia was a daughter to Roman Magistrate Aufidius Lurco and her mother is unknown. She had married Marcus Livius Drusus Claudianus, a future praetor. Their daughter Livia Drusilla was born in 58 BC, however it is unknown whether
2 CONC  they had any other children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aufidia would be the maternal grandmother to Roman Emperor Tiberius and Roman General Nero Claudius Drusus. The Emperors Caligula, Claudius, and Nero were her direct descendants
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Aufidia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Aufidia or Alfidia (flourished 1st century BC) was a woman of Ancient Rome. She was a daughter to Roman Magistrate Marcus Aufidius Lurco and an unknown mother. She was a member of the gens Aufidia, a Roman family of Plebs status w
2 CONC hich appeared in the Roman Republic and Roman Empire, and became a family of consular rank. Her father originally came from Fundi (modern Fondi, Italy).
2 CONT
2 CONT She married the future praetor, Marcus Livius Drusus Claudianus. They had at least two children: a daughter Livia Drusilla (58 BC-29) and a son Marcus Livius Drusus Libo, who served as a Roman consul. Livia was to become the first
2 CONC  Roman Empress and third wife of the first Roman Emperor Augustus. Aufidia would be the maternal grandmother to Roman emperor Tiberius Claudius Nero and Roman General Nero Claudius Drusus. The Roman emperors Caligula, Claudius and
2 CONC  Nero were her direct descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Literature and popular culture'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah Moore appears as Alfidia, the mother of a fictionalized Livia, in two 2007 episodes of the HBO/BBC series Rome. In A Necessary Fiction, she is present when a married Livia catches the eye of young Octavian, and both women 
2 CONC are pleased when he insists that Livia divorce her current husband to marry him. Later, in De Patre Vostro, Alfidia lightly questions Octavian's sister Octavia's loyalty to her family at dinner, and is present when Octavian's moth
2 CONC er Atia of the Julii has an altercation with daughter-in-law Livia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aufidia
