2 CONC idates VI and Mithridates Chrestus. The brothers of Laodice were both under aged to rule and their mother retained all power as regent. Laodice VI’s regency over Pontus was from 120–116 BC (even perhaps up to 113 BC). Laodice VI f
2 CONC avored Mithridates Chrestus over Mithridates VI. During her mother’s regency, Mithridates VI had escaped from the plotting of their mother and had gone into hiding.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mithridates VI between 116–113 BC returned to Pontus from hiding and was hailed King. He was able to remove their mother and brother from the Pontian throne, thus Mithridates VI became the sole ruler of Pontus. Mithridates VI show
