2 CONT on Rome, deserted him, and his son, Pharnaces II, rose up against him
2 CONT declaring himself King. Mithridates commanded his personal bodyguard to accept
2 CONT hisKin son as their king, and retired to a castle where he had himself killed.
2 CONT King of Pontus, as Mithradates VI , in northeastern Anatolia, Asia Minor
2 CONT 0121-0063 f Kr. King of the Bosphorus 0107-0063 B.C
