2 CONC own expense, a vast amount of grain to compensate for a weak inundation.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Legacy'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ptolemy III's reign was also marked by trade with other contemporaneous polities. In the 1930s, excavations by Mattingly at a fortress close to Port Dunford (the likely Nikon of antiquity) in present-day southern Somalia yielded a
2 CONC  number of Ptolemaic coins. Among these pieces were 17 copper mints from the Ptolemy III to Ptolemy V dynasties, as well as late Imperial Rome and Mamluk Sultanate coins.
