1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Magas of Macedon=
2 CONT
2 CONT Magas (Greek: Mάγας) was a Greek Macedonian nobleman that lived in the 4th century BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magas was a local nobleman from obscure origins and was from Eordeaea.[1] Little is known on his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magas married the noblewoman Antigone, the child of Cassander and the niece of the powerful Regent Antipater.[2] His marriage to Antigone reveals that Magas was a nobleman of some social status and influence as he married a close 
2 CONC relation to the powerful Regent and his wife was a distant collateral relative to the Argead dynasty.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT After Magas married Antigone, they settled in Eordeaea. Antigone bore Magas a daughter; his only known child Berenice I of Egypt.[4][5] Magas had two namesakes: his grandson Magas of Cyrene and his great, great grandson Magas of E
2 CONC gypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT References[edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Jump up ^ Ptolemaic Genealogy: Berenice I, Footnote 2
2 CONT 2.Jump up ^ Heckel, Who’s who in the age of Alexander the Great: prosopography of Alexander’s empire, p.71
2 CONT 3.Jump up ^ Ptolemaic Dynasty - Affiliated Lines: The Antipatrids 4.Jump up ^ Heckel, Who’s who in the age of Alexander the Great: prosopography of Alexander’s empire, p.71 5.Jump up ^ Ptolemaic Dynasty - Affiliated Lines: The Ant
2 CONC ipatrids
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources[edit] Ptolemaic Genealogy: Berenice I Ptolemaic Dynasty - Affiliated Lines: Antipatrids W. Heckel, Who’s who in the age of Alexander the Great: prosopography of Alexander’s empire, Wiley-Blackwell, 2006
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magas_of_Macedon
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Magas of Macedon=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Magas (Greek: Mάγας) was a Greek Macedonian nobleman that lived in the 4th century BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magas was a local nobleman from obscure origins and was from Eordeaea. Little is known on his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magas married the noblewoman Antigone, the child of Cassander and the niece of the powerful Regent Antipater. His marriage to Antigone reveals that Magas was a nobleman of some social status and influence as he married a close rel
2 CONC ation to the powerful Regent and his wife was a distant collateral relative to the Argead dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Magas married Antigone, they settled in Eordeaea. Antigone bore Magas a daughter; his only known child Berenice I of Egypt.[4][5] Magas had two namesakes: his grandson Magas of Cyrene and his great, great grandson Magas of E
2 CONC gypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magas_of_Macedon
