1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antigone_of_Macedon Antigone] (Greek: Ἀντιγόνη) was a Greek Macedonian noblewoman that lived in the 4th century BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the child born to the nobleman Cassander by unnamed mother. Antigone was a relative to the powerful Regent Antipater as she was his niece. Her father and paternal uncle were the sons of Iolaus and through her father Antigo
2 CONC ne was a distant collateral relative to the Argead dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antigone was originally from either Paliura or Eordeaea. Little is known on her life. Antigone married a Greek Macedonian nobleman from obscure origins called Magas who was from Eordeaea. Antigone and Magas lived in Eordeaea and h
2 CONC ad a daughter called Berenice I of Egypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT The colony of Antigonia, was named after her and her granddaughter of the same name. Her namesake was the first wife of the Greek King Pyrrhus of Epirus.
