1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Darius II (Persian: داريوش دوم‎‎) (Dārayavahuš), was king of the Persian Empire from 423 BC to 405 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue Darius II was married to the daughter of Gobryas. With the daughter of Gobryas, Darius II had four sons, through whom one of his sons became the father of Artabazanes, who served as King of Media Atropatene in the second hal
2 CONC f of the 3rd century BC.
