1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aristomachus (Ancient Greek: Ἀριστόμαχος) may refer to the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Aristomachus, name of several figure in Greek mythology.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aristomachos the Elder, died 240 BC, a tyrant of the ancient Greek city of Argos. Aristomachos of Argos, died 223 BC, second son of the previous, a tyrant of the city of Argos and strategos of the Achaean League. Aristomachus of C
2 CONC roton, c. 215 BC, a democratic leader who betrayed the town of Croton in Magna Graecia.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the Heracleidae, son of Cleodaeus, a great-grandson of Heracles. He led an attempt to capture Mycenae during the reign of Tisamenus, but, having misinterpreted the oracle, failed and fell in the battle.[2][3] He is the fath
2 CONC er of Temenus, Cresphontes and Aristodemus.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pausanias, Description of Greece, 2. 18. 7 Jump up ^ Herodotus, Histories, 6. 52
